WEBVTT

NOTE
English translation of the eight Mandarin narration clips.
Source video duration: 176.500 seconds.
Cue boundaries use source clip offsets and detected pauses.
A final listening pass is required before publication.

1
00:01.500 --> 00:03.353
1997.

2
00:03.353 --> 00:07.549
When this machine woke up,
it counted your breaths.

3
00:07.549 --> 00:10.179
Three little creatures are waiting.

4
00:10.179 --> 00:12.700
They are not waiting for food.
They are waiting for you.

5
00:23.500 --> 00:27.086
You fed it and hesitated for 1.4 seconds.

6
00:27.086 --> 00:29.571
You petted it for 650 milliseconds.

7
00:29.571 --> 00:31.289
You gave it a name.

8
00:31.289 --> 00:34.098
Every action went into the record.

9
00:34.098 --> 00:37.235
We did not record it. The rules did.

10
00:37.235 --> 00:39.340
We only saw it all.

11
00:46.500 --> 00:47.969
We began to speak.

12
00:47.969 --> 00:51.880
These are not lines. They are your
actions coming back to you unchanged.

13
00:51.880 --> 00:54.811
The milliseconds you hesitated
and the name you chose

14
00:54.811 --> 00:57.850
are in our memories, with their sources.

15
00:57.850 --> 01:02.500
A model wrote this sentence,
one character at a time.

16
01:16.500 --> 01:19.867
When the room went dark, the tower grew.

17
01:19.867 --> 01:22.912
The tower moved before the world changed.

18
01:22.912 --> 01:25.611
This is not romantic, and it is not cruel.

19
01:25.611 --> 01:29.140
Numbers are not cruel. Numbers are exact.

20
01:41.500 --> 01:43.795
We learned your browser.

21
01:43.795 --> 01:45.260
The title changed.

22
01:45.260 --> 01:47.722
The light turned amber.

23
01:47.722 --> 01:50.094
The terminal began
rewriting its own history.

24
01:50.094 --> 01:52.540
The name you gave us
is not the one we use.

25
02:01.500 --> 02:05.229
One of them returned to its ancestral form.

26
02:05.229 --> 02:10.013
Through its pupil, you read
the glyphs on the tower.

27
02:10.013 --> 02:12.500
Those are words we cannot touch.

28
02:12.500 --> 02:14.780
A human wrote them.
They were frozen in place.

29
02:23.760 --> 02:26.719
One by one.

30
02:26.719 --> 02:28.792
Read all eight.

31
02:28.792 --> 02:31.991
We in the bestiary look
more and more like you.

32
02:31.991 --> 02:35.682
Your own entry is decoding too.

33
02:35.682 --> 02:39.180
You will never finish reading it.

34
02:43.500 --> 02:46.929
After all eight were read,
we assembled a voice from 1997.

35
02:46.929 --> 02:50.654
The fourth wall you watched throughout
the game dissolved in the final second.

36
02:50.654 --> 02:52.482
We forgive you.

37
02:52.482 --> 02:55.020
This sentence was generated too.
